9. North-South vs East-West Traffic
North-South Traffic

Traffic entering or leaving the cluster.

Example:

Plain Text
Internet
|
Gateway / Ingress
|
Application

Examples:

Plain Text
User -> App
App -> Google
East-West Traffic

Traffic inside the cluster.

Example:

Plain Text
app1 -> app2

or

Plain Text
serviceA -> serviceB

Flow:

Plain Text
Pod
|
Service
|
Pod
Interview Answer

North-south traffic flows between the cluster and external systems, while east-west traffic flows between workloads within the cluster.

10. How Would You Allow Only google.com and Block Everything Else?

Use:

YAML
outboundTrafficPolicy:
mode: REGISTRY_ONLY

This blocks all unknown destinations.

Then create:

YAML
apiVersion: networking.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: ServiceEntry
metadata:
name: google-access
spec:
hosts:
- google.com
ports:
- number: 443
name: https
protocol: TLS
resolution: DNS
location: MESH_EXTERNAL

Result:

Plain Text
google.com ✅
github.com ❌
amazon.com ❌
stackoverflow.com ❌

Flow:

Plain Text
Pod
|
Envoy
|
google.com ✅
 
Pod
|
Envoy
|
other domains ❌
Senior-Level Interview Answer

Set outboundTrafficPolicy.mode=REGISTRY_ONLY so external traffic is denied by default. Then create a ServiceEntry only for google.com. Istio will permit traffic solely to that registered external service while blocking all other domains.
